Fix warnings seen with gcc16.

VariableSizeMeasurement::subspaceIndices only works if the requested
dimension matches that of the VariableMeasurement.  However, this was enforced
only with an assertion, leading to compilation warnings when the function
was instantiated with a bad requested size.

Split into two templates, via a requires clause.  The first is for the
case where the requested dimension is correct, and actually implements
the method.  The second is for the case where the requested dimension
is incorrect, and simply aborts.
